# tools/al/ales_stereo_limit_env_witness.rish — stereo_limit_env: the attack/release brickwall limiter carried into stereo, the linked envelope driving one linked ceiling over time (ALES163).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES163.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-070439_fill-ales163-lotus-stereo-limit-env.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_envelope.rye (ALES160 — the linked envelope, its stereo_env_step reused whole), lotus/stereo_limit.rye (ALES158 — the linked ceiling this drives over time, its memoryless form the unit-coefficient
# limit), lotus/limit_env.rye (ALES55 — the mono attack/release limiter, its LimitEnvError reused whole and its output the left-always-peak comparison), lotus/limit.rye (ALES49 — the hard ceiling),
# lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 — the StereoClip), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_max).
#
# lotus/stereo_limit_env.rye limits a span of sample-PAIRS in a master to a magnitude ceiling, the one gain reduction following the shared LINKED envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope toward the
# linked peak max(|left|, |right|) by ALES160's step (attack while rising, release while falling): within the ceiling both pass byte for byte, above it the single gain ceil/e (in (0, 1)) is applied to both raw samples —
# the compressor at an infinite ratio, the target pinned to the ceiling, one detector, one gain, the image held. On the above-ceiling branch e > ceil >= 1, so the divide is always safe. LimitEnvError (BadCeiling, BadCoeff,
# BadRange) reused whole; the fusion adds no fault. Values only, never a length. The crux is the instantaneous law (unit attack and release reducing it to ALES158's memoryless stereo_limit byte for byte on both — the
# time-varying rung's zero-smoothing limit is exactly the memoryless one already proven), the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with left' equal to ALES55's mono limit_env(left), the right scaled by the
# same fraction, the independent per-channel limit_env differing), the image law (the shared gain preserving the L:R ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase), the knob / no-lookahead law (below the ceiling the
# identity, a slower attack letting the transient overshoot, an instant attack pinning the peak-holder on the ceiling), the carry law (a span in two pieces equal to the whole once on both), and the sub-ceiling/silence/balance/
# atomicity/degenerate law.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_limit_env_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-limit-env: Language EN — stereo_limit_env limits a span of sample-pairs in a stereo master to a magnitude ceiling, the one gain reduction following the shared linked envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope toward the linked peak (the max of the two channels' magnitudes, clamped to the rail), the attack fraction while it rises and the release while it falls; where the smoothed envelope sits within the ceiling both channels pass byte for byte, and where it rises above, the single gain (the ceiling over the envelope, in the open interval zero to one) is applied to both raw samples. It validates the ceiling, attack, release, and span once against the shared length before any write, so a refusal never limits one channel and leaves the other torn. It writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced; the caller owns the envelope across calls, so a span limited in two pieces equals the whole once."
say "ales-stereo-limit-env: Style Radiant — ALES158's stereo_limit pins a pair the instant it crosses the ceiling: the peak lands exactly on the ceiling the moment it arrives, and the pinning vanishes the moment the pair falls. A real limiter breathes — it approaches the ceiling over an attack and releases the gain gently afterward. ALES160 built exactly that breath for stereo, one shared envelope tracking the linked peak, and proved it once. This rung spends both proofs: it drives the gain reduction from the smoothed linked envelope rather than the bare pair, and applies the one resulting gain to both channels — the compressor at an infinite ratio, the envelope's target pinned exactly to the ceiling, the image held to the sample the whole time. Two proofs fused: the detector is linked and time-smoothed (the louder channel deciding the shared loudness over time), and the gain is linked (one gain from the linked envelope applied to both, since limiting each channel by its own envelope would reduce on different samples and shift the image). The crux is six laws: the instantaneous law (unit attack and release making the linked envelope the instantaneous linked peak, so this equals ALES158's memoryless stereo_limit byte for byte on both — the time-varying rung's zero-smoothing limit exactly the memoryless one already proven); the linked-gain-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with the left equal to ALES55's mono limit_env of it byte for byte, the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel limit_env genuinely differing); the image law (the shared gain preserving the left-to-right ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase, no magnitude expanding and no sign flipping); the knob and no-lookahead law (below the ceiling the identity, a slower attack letting a fast transient briefly overshoot the ceiling before the envelope catches it, a gain-reducer over time rather than a sample-clamp, an instant attack pinning the peak-holding channel exactly on the ceiling); the carry law (a span limited in two pieces equal to limiting the whole once, byte for byte on both); and the sub-ceiling, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate law (a master whose linked envelope never crosses the ceiling passing byte for byte, silence staying silence, the lengths held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-limit-env: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) carrying one shared i64 envelope, one linked-peak comparison and at most one multiply-then-divide for the envelope step (ALES160's proven stereo_env_step) plus one per channel for the gain, all in i64 (the product of a magnitude and the ceiling at most 32767 times 32767 never overflowing), the gain ceiling over e in the open interval zero to one so every scaled magnitude is at most its input's and fits i16; the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (a limiter writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit, each written sign asserted held); the ceiling, both coefficients, and the span are validated once before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never limits one channel and leaves the other torn; the linked envelope is asserted a legal magnitude in zero to sample_max each sample and the gain applies only where e exceeds the ceiling (so e is at least one greater than the ceiling and the divide is always safe — the zero-envelope case the gate faced cannot arise here); StereoLimitEnvError is ALES55's LimitEnvError (BadCeiling, BadCoeff, BadRange) reused whole, the fusion adding no fault. The instantaneous law is proven by running both stereo_limit_env under unit attack and release and ALES158's memoryless stereo_limit on the same master and demanding byte-for-byte equality on both channels; the linked-gain-over-time law against a master where the left always holds the peak — the left equal to ALES55's mono limit_env of it byte for byte while the right is scaled by the same fraction, the independent mono limit_env of the right alone shown to genuinely differ; the image law proves no magnitude expands and no sign flips over a mixed master and that an out-of-phase pair returns still exactly out of phase; the knob and no-lookahead law proves below the ceiling the identity, a slower attack letting the first onset sample overshoot where an instant attack pins it exactly on the ceiling; the carry law proves a span limited in two pieces equal to the whole once on both channels; and the silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove an all-silent master staying zero, the length held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the ceiling a magnitude in sample units, the attack and release fractions per sample index, no lookahead, no real sample rate, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_limit_env"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_limit_env.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-limit-env: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_limit_env.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-limit-env: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-limit-env: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-limit-env' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-limit-env: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-limit-env line"
